# Written for this pack by BurN-30 (GPL-3.0). Quest ids, givers, places and levels from
# Polestar's Forever data (data-v2026.11.1: QuestieDB Forever, the 1.60.1 client) and its
# Dungeons codex; boss order, quest drops and tips from Wowhead Forever (quest, NPC and zone
# pages, its Deadmines guide and the comments, read on 2026-11-08), rewritten. Not played in
# game yet.
#
# Optional chapter: the first step asks once (`when group 132`, Polestar's "Skip it / Do it
# with a group" banner) and every later step needs it done (`when done dm-start`). Skipped,
# over level 24, or without The Defias Brotherhood (65) handed in to Wiley in Lakeshire
# (07-carmines): the whole chapter is left out and Duskwood follows.
#
# Flow: Lakeshire (Wiley) -> Sentinel Hill (Gryan) -> Stormwind (Shaw, Thistlenettle, Shoni,
# Sprite Jumpsprocket, Jasper Fel) -> Sentinel Hill (the Messenger, the Traitor's escort, Alba
# Fairmoon) -> Moonbrook: the undead outside, then the Deadmines boss by boss -> the cove exit
# (Alba) -> Sentinel Hill -> Stormwind rewards.
guide groupe-alliance/07b-mortemines
title Group 6b · The Deadmines (dungeon 18-23, optional)
folder Group Alliance
category Dungeons
faction Alliance
levels 20-23
zone Redridge Mountains
next groupe-alliance/08-bois-de-la-penombre

step Lakeshire: Wiley the Black
  label dm-start
  when group 132
  when turnedin 65
  when level<25
  tip The Deadmines: a 5-player dungeon under Moonbrook, in Westfall, best at 18 to 23. This chapter takes its quests on the way, then the dungeon boss by boss. Alone? Skip it: the guide goes on to Duskwood.
  note Keep 8 free quest log slots. Everyone takes the quests at their own pace; meet at the Moonbrook entrance for the run.
  accept 132                                  -- Wiley the Black, upstairs in the inn

step Sentinel Hill
  when done dm-start
  zone Westfall
  fly "Sentinel Hill"
  turnin 132                                  -- Gryan Stoutmantle
  accept 135

step Stormwind
  when done dm-start
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Fly to Stormwind. Mathias Shaw is upstairs at SI:7 in Old Town, Jasper Fel in the same building; Wilder Thistlenettle (tavern), Shoni the Shilent and Sprite Jumpsprocket are in the Dwarven District. Train while you are here.
  fly "Stormwind"
  turnin 135                                  -- Master Mathias Shaw
  accept 141
  accept 168                                  -- Wilder Thistlenettle
  accept 167
  accept 2040 optional                        -- Shoni the Shilent
  accept 92749 optional                       -- Sprite Jumpsprocket: only after Explosive Consultation, from Alba in Westfall
  accept 92750 optional
  turnin 92750 optional                       -- Jasper Fel, SI:7
  accept 92751 optional
  turnin 92751 optional                       -- Sprite Jumpsprocket
  buy 4358 x10 optional                       -- Rough Dynamite (not Coarse, whatever the text says): Auction House or an engineer friend
  turnin 92749 optional
  accept 92752 optional                       -- For Alba Fairmoon in Westfall

step Sentinel Hill
  when done dm-start
  zone Westfall
  fly "Sentinel Hill"
  turnin 141                                  -- Gryan Stoutmantle
  accept 142

step The Defias Messenger
  when done dm-start
  tip He walks the road from the Moonbrook smithy to the Gold Coast Quarry and the Jangolode Mine, and back: wait for him by the smithy. He runs at low health and can drag Moonbrook's Defias along: root or slow him and finish him fast.
  collect 1381 quest 142 @45.1,69.3           -- A Mysterious Message: Defias Messenger

step Sentinel Hill
  when done dm-start
  turnin 142                                  -- Gryan Stoutmantle
  accept 155                                  -- The Defias Traitor, at the foot of the tower ramp
  turnin 92752 optional                       -- Alba Fairmoon
  accept 92753 optional

step Escort the Defias Traitor
  when done dm-start
  tip He walks to Moonbrook. The hard spot is the fountain: a Defias by the cart and the caster at the fountain join in, so deal with the caster first (Polymorph, Fear). Clearing Moonbrook beforehand makes it easy alone at 18.
  note Not there? Someone is escorting him: wait for him to come back, or group up with them. Since 05/11 he can vanish when crossing a zone border (a known bug, fix on the way): abandon and take the quest again.
  complete 155                                -- Escort him to Moonbrook

step Sentinel Hill
  when done dm-start
  turnin 155                                  -- Gryan Stoutmantle
  accept 166
  accept 214                                  -- Scout Riell, at the top of the tower

step The mine outside the portal
  when done dm-start
  tip Moonbrook's smithy hides the mine. Before the portal, the purple area of the minimap holds elite undead miners in pairs: the Miners' Union Cards drop there, not inside, and Foreman Thistlenettle stands at the far end with a linked add.
  note Alone: around 20-21 for the cards, 23 for the Foreman. Two players: fine at 19-20. The cards drop rarely and each player loots their own: skip them if time runs short.
  collect 1894 quest 168                      -- Miners' Union Card: Undead Excavators and Dynamiters, elite
  collect 1875 quest 167 @42.2,82.6           -- Thistlenettle's Badge: Foreman Thistlenettle, elite
  goto 42.5,71.7 "The Deadmines" r 25

step Rhahk'Zor
  when done dm-start
  tip Group of 5, level 18 or more. Pull the two Watchmen away from Rhahk'Zor first, and turn around after every boss: patrols come from behind. Miner Johnson, a rare, may stand in the small tunnel on the left after him: kill his miners first.
  note Share each quest with your group: click it in the quest log, then Share. Red Silk Bandanas drop from Defias all through the dungeon.
  kill 644                                    -- Rhahk'Zor
  collect 915 quest 214                       -- Red Silk Bandana: any Defias

# Groupe Alliance 0.11.0 (review): the Paladin class quest of the codex (The Test of Righteousness,
# 1654), only for Paladins who hold it. Whitestone Oak Lumber: Goblin Woodcarvers (Polestar's
# Forever data, 100 %). The rest of the chain (Shadowfang Keep, Blackfathom Deeps) is in
# Polestar's class guide forever/class/paladin/verigans-fist.
step Paladins: The Test of Righteousness
  only Paladin
  when done dm-start
  when onquest 1654
  along until dm-sneed
  tip The Goblin Woodcarvers of the lumber room, before Sneed's Shredder, drop the Whitestone Oak Lumber. The chain also needs Jordan's Smithing Hammer (Shadowfang Keep, not on this route) and the Kor Gem (Blackfathom Deeps): Polestar's class guides (Verigan's Fist) cover all of it.
  collect 6994 quest 1654                     -- Whitestone Oak Lumber: Goblin Woodcarvers

step Sneed's Shredder and Sneed
  label dm-sneed
  when done dm-start
  tip Clear every Goblin Woodcarver of the lumber room first, pulling them back to the previous room: the Shredder's Terrify sends you running into them. Sneed jumps out when it breaks; he disarms.
  collect 7365 quest 2040 optional            -- Gnoam Sprecklesprocket: Sneed's Shredder
  kill 643                                    -- Sneed

step Gilnid's foundry
  when done dm-start
  tip Goblin Engineers and Craftsmen summon golems: kill or stun the goblin, the golem goes with it. Gilnid has an Engineer at his side. Plant the explosives near the middle of the room before pulling him.
  complete 92753 optional                     -- Place the explosives, near the middle of the foundry
  kill 1763                                   -- Gilnid

step The cannon door
  when done dm-start
  tip The Defias Gunpowder barrel sits in the alcove on the right just before the cannon. Fire the cannon, then step back: a patrol of elites comes out through the broken door. A Rogue can pick the lock instead.
  task "The cannon door is open" optional

step Mr. Smite
  when done dm-start
  tip In the cove: two stealthed Defias Blackguards join him by the walkway, kill them before he reaches 66%. At 66% and 33% he stuns the whole group for a few seconds and changes weapons: keep the tank's health up before each.
  kill 646                                    -- Mr. Smite

step Captain Greenskin
  when done dm-start
  tip On the ship. Crowd-control the Squallshaper, kill the Companion, then the Pirate, then Greenskin facing away from the group (Cleave).
  kill 647                                    -- Captain Greenskin

step Edwin VanCleef
  when done dm-start
  tip Captain's cabin, top of the ship. Two Blackguards join at the pull, two more at half health: a stun at 51 to 55% skips the second pair. Everyone on the quest loots their own head and their own letter.
  collect 3637 quest 166                      -- Head of VanCleef
  accept 373 item 2874                        -- An Unsent Letter, on VanCleef: right-click it, it opens the Stockade chain
  note Cookie, on the lower deck, is optional: interrupt his healing cast. Do not hearth: leave by the back, along the coast.

step The cove exit: Alba Fairmoon
  when done dm-start
  tip Out by the back of the cove; Alba waits right outside with the Detonator. No item reward on this chain: XP and reputation.
  turnin 92753 optional                       -- Alba Fairmoon
  accept 92819 optional
  interact 581792 quest 92819 optional        -- The Detonator, beside her
  turnin 92819 optional

step Sentinel Hill rewards
  when done dm-start
  turnin 166                                  -- Gryan Stoutmantle
  turnin 214                                  -- Scout Riell, top of the tower

step Stormwind rewards
  when done dm-start
  zone Stormwind City
  fly "Stormwind"
  turnin 168                                  -- Wilder Thistlenettle, Dwarven District
  turnin 167
  turnin 2040 optional                        -- Shoni the Shilent
  turnin 373                                  -- Baros Alexston, Cathedral Square
  accept 389                                  -- For Warden Thelwater: the Stockade, after Duskwood
  note Duskwood next: fly to Darkshire if you know its flight path, else ride south through Elwynn.
